SCOPE — CODE vs. CONTENT (please read)

The MIT license above covers the SOFTWARE only: the pipeline code, scripts,
web player, and documentation in this repository (e.g. pipeline/, scripts/,
docs/app/, docs/*.html, docs/playbook/, the build recipes and maps under
data/books, data/chapter_maps, data/repairs).

It does NOT cover the CONTENT — the source texts and the audio/companion
editions derived from them. Those remain the property of their respective
copyright holders, or are in the public domain, on their own terms:

  • Source texts and rendered audiobooks of papal encyclicals (e.g. the files
    under data/sources/ and docs/audio/, and the text in docs/guide,
    docs/transcript, docs/text) are © Libreria Editrice Vaticana, reproduced
    here freely, non-commercially, with attribution, and not sold separately,
    per the Holy See's stated permission. The authoritative originals are
    published at vatican.va.

  • Works that are in the public domain by age (e.g. Rerum Novarum, 1891) are
    free of copyright as works; specific modern translations may not be.

  • Any future text added to this library carries its own rights; see each
    book's recipe (data/books/<id>.json "rights") and the copyright &
    permissions playbook in docs/WORK-QUEUE.md.

In short: you are free to reuse the MACHINERY under MIT; the BOOKS are not the
project's to relicense, and your use of them is governed by their own rights.
This notice is informational, not legal advice.
